    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented telephone normalization on owner creation (`POST /api/owners`) using the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in this repo.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **New step `NormalizeTelephone`** (`.../function/owner/NormalizeTelephone.java`) \u2014 reads the republished `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, strips every non-digit character (`replaceAll(\"\\\\D\", \"\")`), and requires exactly 10 digits. It writes the normalized value back onto the same DTO object (mutate-in-place, so the later `BuildOwner` step maps the 10-digit value into the entity that gets stored and returned as `telephone`). Non-10-digit input throws a checked `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`InvalidTelephoneException`** (checked, `extends Exception`) so it surfaces as an OfficeFloor escalation.\n\n3. **Escalation handler + YAML** \u2014 `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler` responds `400 Bad Request`, wired via `officefloor/escalation/...InvalidTelephoneException.yml`.\n\n4. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted the `normalize` step into `owners.POST.yml` between `require` and `build` (`require \u2192 normalize \u2192 build \u2192 save \u2192 respond`), under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n**Why this placement:** `RequireOwnerFields` binds the body (the single `@RequestBody` step) without `@Valid`, so the raw `(04) 1234-5678` passes binding; blank-check runs first; then normalization strips to `0412345678`, which satisfies the entity's `@Pattern(^[0-9]{10}$)` on persist. Too-few-digits (`12345`) is rejected with 400 before the entity is built.\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass: `coreStripsToTenDigits` (`(04) 1234-5678` \u2192 stored/returned as `0412345678`) and `errorRejectsTooFewDigits` (`12345` \u2192 400).",
